## Anti Patterns (Các pattern cần tránh)

### 1. Anemic Domain Model
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Anemic model - just data
class Order {
  id: string;
  status: string;
  items: any[];
  
  getStatus() { return this.status; }
  setStatus(status) { this.status = status; }
}

// ✅ GOOD: Rich domain model
class Order {
  private status: OrderStatus;
  
  complete(): void {
    if (this.status !== OrderStatus.VALIDATED) {
      throw new DomainException('Order must be validated before completion');
    }
    this.status = OrderStatus.COMPLETED;
  }
}
```

### 2. God Aggregate
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Everything in one aggregate
class HugeAggregate {
  // 50 entities, 100 methods
  // Too many invariants, huge transaction
}

// ✅ GOOD: Small, focused aggregates
class OrderAggregate {
  // Only order-related logic
  // Other entities in separate aggregates
}
```

### 3. Anemic Value Objects
```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Mutable address
class Address {
  street: string;
  city: string;
  // Setters...
}

// ✅ GOOD: Immutable address
class Address {
  constructor(
    public readonly street: string,
    public readonly city: string,
    public readonly country: Country
  ) {
    Object.freeze(this);
  }
  
  changeStreet(newStreet: string): Address {
    return new Address(newStreet, this.city, this.country);
  }
}
```

## Best Practices (Thực hành tốt nhất)

1. **Start strategic, then tactical**: Define contexts before modeling
2. **Keep aggregates small**: Single aggregate per consistency boundary
3. **Use value objects for descriptions**: Immutable, interchangeable
4. **Protect aggregate invariants**: Only aggregate root can modify
5. **Use domain events for cross-boundary communication**
6. **Define bounded contexts by team ownership**: Conway's Law
7. **Avoid big balls of mud**: Clear context boundaries
8. **Use ubiquitous language**: Shared vocabulary in code and business
9. **Design for autonomy**: Contexts should be independently deployable
10. **Iterate on the model**: Continuous refinement with domain experts

